From: lean <chenlin@fnnas.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kbuild: retain built-in module metadata through garbage collection

The ARM link uses --gc-sections. Preserve .modinfo until Kbuild extracts
modules.builtin.modinfo from vmlinux.unstripped; the final image stripping
still removes the metadata. Otherwise modules.builtin is empty and the
OpenWrt package builder mistakes built-in drivers for missing modules.

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>

--- a/include/asm-generic/vmlinux.lds.h
+++ b/include/asm-generic/vmlinux.lds.h
@@ -838,7 +838,7 @@
 		.shstrtab 0 : { *(.shstrtab) }
 
 #define MODINFO								\
-		.modinfo : { *(.modinfo) . = ALIGN(8); }
+		.modinfo : { KEEP(*(.modinfo)) . = ALIGN(8); }
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_GENERIC_BUG
 #define BUG_TABLE							\
